  "notes": "A compound verb formed from ⟦{消|き}える→消える：02520_kieru⟧ (to disappear) + ⟦{去|さ}る→去る：02115_saru⟧ (to leave, to go away). The ⟦{去|さ}る→去る：02115_saru⟧ component adds emphasis on the completeness and finality of the disappearance. Godan verb conjugation: {消|き}え{去|さ}らない (negative), {消|き}え{去|さ}った (past). Can be used for both physical things (fog, people) and abstract things (memories, feelings, pain). More literary in tone than ⟦{消|き}える→消える：02520_kieru⟧ alone.",
